{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/65","id":4687432801,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABF2SMYQ","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/65","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/65.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/65.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/65","number":65,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Construct a reviewed explicit Blaschke product with Bloch Cayley transform","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Explicit construction\n\nAn explicit answer to Holland's Problem 5.51 (AMR-022-5051): a deterministic four-adic integer recursion produces rational finite Blaschke products B_n with algebraic coefficients. Their locally uniform limit B is an infinite Blaschke product with B(0)=0 and Bloch Cayley transform (1+B)/(1-B).\n\nThe construction includes the quantitative bound\n\n`sup_{|z|<=r} |B(z)-B_n(z)| <= 4*pi*r*4^(-n)/(1-r)^2`.\n\nThe proof separately excludes a singular inner factor. The absorbed unit-step densities cannot converge to a finite positive value at any boundary point; Loomis's positive-measure converse Fatou theorem would force exactly such convergence if a singular factor were present. A proved global Zygmund estimate gives the Bloch property.\n\n## Scope and prior work\n\n- The complete explicit recursion and proof are in `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/2305051/CANDIDATE.md`\n- This is a recursive rational-inner construction with an effective compact-uniform error bound, not a short closed-form zero list\n- Existence and stronger covering-map results were already known\n- Kahane's and Cantón's martingale methods and all classical analytic inputs are credited\n- Historical priority is unestablished\n\n## Separate validation\n\nThe unchanged independent adversarial review passes the complete construction and the source's explicitness requirement, including the singular-factor argument and exact disk normalization.\n\n- 2,884 author exact assertions, reproduced byte-for-byte\n- 37,154 independent exact controls, reproduced byte-for-byte\n- Frozen candidate SHA-256: `0a15d03ab92cbd13f17042a4708f75c3d592f4884810c7ffadc6a5f34f1cb6c4`\n\nThe finite controls support, but do not replace, the all-stage and analytic proof. This is separate AI review, not human peer review. Please keep this PR open as a draft for further examination.\n","created_at":"2026-09-30T07:37:01Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T07:39:06Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"62936f5c992c85161641e12b732ac2b57023faec","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/65/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/65/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/65/comments","statuses_url":"https://a